! mcp_bootstrap_p327.strap -- MCP printed page 327: the LOADER's
! relocation-segment tail (ARNRM5, ARNRM3 library branch, ARNRM4) and
! the opening of the OCTAL CARD LOADER (AOCTAL .. AOCTL1), lines 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.78, read at 400 dpi, doubtful glyphs
! at 900 dpi.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 22LOADER  CARD
! ID TA000351  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 327"; the heading row's
! LOCATION field is 235010, line 1's word.  NOTE the PUNID: 22LOADER,
! not 11D11MCP.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines; every line number prints a "*" after it.  No
! TAIL card.  Located rows run contiguous from 235010.00 (line 1) to
! 235052.00 (line 50, BRZ, a half word; next location 235052.40), then
! blank paper.  "*" after the LOCATION on lines 14, 30 and 47.
!   line 31  remark card, "-" in the NAME field, "OCTAL CARD LOADER".
! JOIN.  p.326 has no scratch neighbour; contiguity with it is NOT
! established here.  p.328 should open at 235052.40 with serial
! TA000401.
!
! EXTERNALS.  KSILO and the ALL bits / ALB / ATWSTA are landed (p.171,
! p.291); stand-ins are checked by the merge.  Every other value comes
! from this page's binary; each comment says how much it fixes.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * LINE 19'S BYTE PRINTS "C8" AND IS 08.  At 900 dpi the first glyph
!     is the same open round this drum prints for 0 in the octal field
!     one row up (".C3").  C-I's byte is 08 in every landed C-I row, and
!     the landed row 217123.00 (G EMAN C-I,$4,0.0) prints the
!     same "C8" and was written 08.
!   * line 21 "YRLCTA" = YRLDTA: line 25 prints the same symbol (same
!     address 235307.00) with the D stem; volume OCR reads YRLDTA twice.
!   * line 46 "CTIC110" = CTI0110 (connective digits; the immediate
!     form, as landed decks write CTI0110/CTI0001).
!   * "CMOCOO" (lines 6, 35) = CM0000; "C($1)" (line 24) = 0($1);
!     "KVI,$1,C" (line 8) = 0; "KSILC" read KSILO (landed p.171).
!   * A-names spelled with an open round after A (ACCTAL, ACCTLA,
!     ACCTLD, ACCTL1/2/5/6, ACCTZ, ACXW1/2, ACIGN2, ACIGNR) written O:
!     C22-6728 prints AOCTAL, AOCTLA, AOCTL and AOIGNI; the family is
!     the octal loader's.  O vs digit 0 is NOT settled by ink for the
!     AOXW pair (the sheet read A0XW1 once).
!   * "ANORMR" (line 34) as printed: C22-6728 "routines return to
!     ANORMR to make a normal return ... ANORMR returns control to
!     APCRDND" (this line's remark).  C22-6728's ANORMP is a different
!     program's label (panel dump).
!   * octal / hex fields with an open round read 0 ("FC"/"FO" = F0,
!     "CO"/"C0" in octal fields = 00).  The "C0" byte of line 48 and the
!     "C2" bytes of lines 9 and 50 are what BZRZ/BXE/BRZ assemble.
!
! >>> LINE 6 FAILS, AND IT IS THE ASSEMBLER, NOT THE INK. <<<
! "CM0000,AFPCI" prints 232543.11 80 000400.00 F0: length 64 (field 0)
! and BYTE SIZE 4 -- ALL's (N) dds (p.291 line 9 "ALL DRZ(N),1")
! reaching the connective through "AFPCI SYN,ALL.9" (p.291 line 17).  A
! second witness of the (N)-connective rule (printed p.267 line 1), and
! the first that the dds carries through a SYN to "SYMBOL.bit" (C22-6531
! printed p.11: an expression takes its FINAL symbol's dds).  strap_asm
! inherits dds through SYN only for a BARE symbol (the sym_dds branch
! after "A SYN TO A BARE SYMBOL INHERITS", ~line 2837), so AFPCI gets no
! dds and the row assembles 000000.00 F0.  Measured: AFPCI written
! SYN(N), (8)232543.11 passes, but that would give AFPCI a second dds
! against p.291's defining SYN and the merge refuses it; so the printed
! defining form is kept and the row is left failing.  ALL's stand-in
! carries (N) as p.267's YC1DB SYN(N) does (ALL is placed by p.291).
!
! SPELLINGS read at 900 dpi: AREADS (S, not 5) and AREAD1 (lines 13,
! 26); AOIGN2 (2, not Z: compare AOCTL2) and AOCTZ (Z as in BZRZ);
! AOCTL6 (6, not O).  The glyph after A in the AO- names prints with a
! straight-ish left side on lines 43-50; C22-6728's typeset AOCTAL /
! AOCTLA / AOIGNI and p.291's AOIGNI decide O.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  TA000351 .. TA000400, one per line, none shared, none
! skipped.

KSILO   SYN, (8)220451.0             ! landed p.171 DR(BU,64); SV line 10 KSILO+9.32
ALL     SYN(N), (8)232543.0          ! landed p.291 line 9 DRZ(N),1; dds carried so AFPCI inherits it (line 6)
AFPCI   SYN,ALL.9                    ! landed p.291 line 17
AOIGNI  SYN,ALL.5                    ! landed p.291 line 13
APCRDI  SYN,ALL.6                    ! landed p.291 line 14
ADCRDI  SYN,ALL.8                    ! landed p.291 line 16
ALB     SYN, (8)232547.71            ! landed p.291 line 29 (A*)DD(BU,12,6)
ATWSTA  SYN, (8)232550.05            ! landed p.291 line 30 (A*)DD(BU,48,6)
AREADS  SYN(BU), (8)235246.0         ! not landed; LX line 13 235246.32, half word only
AREAD1  SYN(BU), (8)235245.0         ! not landed; LX line 26 235245.32, half word only
YRLDTA  SYN, (8)235307.0             ! not landed; SF lines 21, 25 235307.00, BIT-EXACT
AOCTL5  SYN, (8)235064.40            ! not landed; SVA line 33 AOCTL5+.32 = 235065.00, BIT-EXACT
ANORMR  SYN, (8)235233.0             ! not landed; CM1111 line 34 ANORMR.19 = 235233.23, BIT-EXACT
AOCTL2  SYN, (8)235054.40            ! not landed; SVA line 37 235054.47 / LVI line 36 AOCTL2+1. 235055.47, BIT-EXACT
AOXW1   SYN(BU), (8)235247.0         ! not landed; LX line 38 235247.02, half word only
AOXW2   SYN(BU), (8)235250.0         ! not landed; LX line 40 235250.04, half word only
AOIGN2  SYN, (8)235107.0             ! not landed; BB line 43 235107.34, half word only
AOIGNR  SYN, (8)235106.0             ! not landed; BBZ line 47 235106.34, half word only
AOCTL6  SYN, (8)235122.40            ! not landed; BZRZ line 48 235122.74, half word only
AOCTZ   SYN, (8)235103.0             ! not landed; BRZ line 50 235103.34, half word only

        SLC, (8)235010.00
        BXCZ,ARNRM5                                          ! line  1  -NO TRANSFER VECTOR TO TRANSMIT
        V+,$1,2.($1)                                         ! line  2  -COMPUTE LOC. OF T.V. IN RELOC. TABLE
        V+I,$1,3.                                            ! line  3
        T,$2,0($1),1.($2)                                    ! line  4
ARNRM5  Z,$1                                                 ! line  5
        CM0000,AFPCI                                         ! line  6
        SR,$2,$1                                             ! line  7
        KVI,$1,0                                             ! line  8  -ANY MORE SEGMENTS TO BE LOADED
        BXE,ARNRM4                                           ! line  9  -NO-BRANCH
        SV,$1,KSILO+9.32                                     ! line 10  -STORE ADDR. OF NEXT RELOCATION TABLE
        BB,.63($1),ARNRM3                                    ! line 11  -LIBRARY ROUTINE  BRANCH
        L(BU,18),($1),-18                                    ! line 12
        LX,$13,AREADS                                        ! line 13  -SET UP $13 FOR RESLD
        V+,$13,$L                                            ! line 14
        LFI(BU,9),0,-9                                       ! line 15
        /I(BU,18),15.,-18                                    ! line 16
        LV,1,$L                                              ! line 17
        SVA,1,$.32                                           ! line 18
        C-I,13,$                                             ! line 19
        LF(BU,48,6),ATWSTA                                   ! line 20
        SF(BU,48,6),YRLDTA                                   ! line 21
        B,3.32($15)                                          ! line 22
ARNRM3  LF(BU,12,6),ALB,48                                   ! line 23  -SET UP RESLD FOR LIB SUBROUTINE
        LF(BU,36,6),0($1)                                    ! line 24
        SF(BU,48,6),YRLDTA                                   ! line 25
        LX,$13,AREAD1                                        ! line 26
        B,3.32($15)                                          ! line 27
ARNRM4  LV,$1,KSILO+10.                                      ! line 28
        SVA,$1,3.($15)                                       ! line 29
        B,2.32($15)                                          ! line 30
! line 31  - OCTAL CARD LOADER
AOCTAL  LVI,$1,AOCTLD                                        ! line 32  -INITIALIZE FOR C CARDS
        SVA,$1,AOCTL5+.32                                    ! line 33
        CM1111(BU,1),ANORMR.19                               ! line 34  -SET BRANCH TO APCRDND TO NOP
        CM0000(BU,1),.57($15)                                ! line 35
AOCTLA  LVI,$3,AOCTL2+1.                                     ! line 36  -INITIALIZE FOR C AND P CARDS
        SVA,$3,AOCTL2                                        ! line 37
        LX,$1,AOXW1                                          ! line 38  -XR1 LOCATED COLUMN BEING TESTED
        LVI,$3,0                                             ! line 39  -USED FOR CONTINUATION C AND P CARDS
        LX,$2,AOXW2                                          ! line 40  -STORAGE AREA FOR CONVERTED COLUMNS
        LCI,$3,4                                             ! line 41  -MAX. NO. OF HALFWDS PER CARD
AOCTLD  LF(BU,12),.70($1)                                    ! line 42  -PUT DECIMAL PT COLUMN IN AC
        BB,AOIGNI,AOIGN2                                     ! line 43  -IF ON IGNORE CORRECTIONS ON CRD
        BB,ADCRDI,$+3.                                       ! line 44
        BB,APCRDI,$+2.                                       ! line 45  -IF P CARD DONT TEST FOR 1
        CTI0110(BU,12),(8)4102                               ! line 46  -TEST FOR DECIMAL POINT
        BBZ,$R+.55,AOIGNR                                    ! line 47  -A 1 BIT IGNORE CORRECTION
        BZRZ,AOCTL6                                          ! line 48  -NOT A DECIMAL POINT
AOCTL1  CT0011(BU,8)(V+I),.12($1)                            ! line 49  -PICK UP AN OCTAL COLUMN
        BRZ,AOCTZ                                            ! line 50  -BLANK COL STORE A ZERO

!SYM ARNRM5 235012.40
!SYM ARNRM3 235027.00
!SYM ARNRM4 235033.00
!SYM AOCTAL 235034.40
